      "alt_text": "One ivory handle with four broad nibs, each touching a separate strip; one nib is muted red.",
      "suggested_caption": "Vectorised arithmetic — a metaphor for a shared operation across several elements; the four contacts are compositional.",
      "metaphor": "One shared four-nib stylus acting across separate strips; the common tool and distinct contact points carry the meaning.",
      "differentiation": "One coordinated operation over several elements rather than transformation through a compiler press, item transport, network fanout or a cell grid.",
      "semantic_caveats": [
        "Nib count is compositional; it does not assert SIMD width, thread count, instruction set or hardware lanes.",
        "Array syntax and vectorised APIs do not alone prove a particular SIMD execution mechanism.",
        "No hardware, performance, energy-efficiency, numerical-equivalence or benchmark claim is encoded.",
        "Four nibs are a requested visual construction, not a measured data count.",
        "The red nib is only an accent: it does not encode a mask, selected lane, numerical state or result."
      ],
